ispatch_lock/claim/_claim_input_refusal/_claim_refusal/_abandoned_claim;commit\"\r\n detail = \"\"\"The claim owns its dispatch-lock discipline and its bookkeeping commit. One claim commit moves one queued specification and cuts its branch; empty or multi-item input refuses before any move, commit, branch or worktree. Historical multi-item claim commits remain readable and are neither split nor re-claimed. The integration restriction retains its existing one-branch refresh behavior.\"\"\"\r\n@@\r\n title = \"The adjudication kind: rank-1 slot + no-bar arm + the bar strictness key\"\r\n-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/schedule.py\"\r\n-code_symbol = \"SAFETY_CLASSES/_KIND_CONCURRENCY/_KIND_RANK\"\r\n+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/schedule.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py\"\r\n+code_symbol = \"SAFETY_CLASSES/_KIND_CONCURRENCY/_KIND_RANK/_lane_bar_directives\"\r\n detail = \"\"\"The adjudication kind remains exclusive at rank 1. A lane whose one claimed row is adjudication runs no product bar; a lane whose one row is any other kind, or whose frontmatter is unreadable, runs the bar. The declared bar key sets that row's verification strictness without affecting scheduling, and a malformed value refuses before refresh.\"\"\"\r\n@@\r\n title = \"The verdict record: what carries a governing verdict, and what binds it to the tree it judged\"\r\n-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py\"\r\n-code_symbol = \"RECORD_PREFIXES/fold_listing/tree_identity/refresh_subject/refresh_attestation/format_bar_green/bar_attestation/tests_digest/mechanical_close_attestation/work_tip/governing_rev/governing_identity/format_trailer/parse_trailer/round_file/session_log/format_scope/gating_span/filing_refusal/branch_paths/logged_rounds/round_entries/branch_entries/tree_already_judged/declared_phases/phases_owed/round_count/format_branch_trailer/branch_trailers;attest/_attest_preflight/_attest_message/_lane_off_trunk/_harness_floor_refusal/_attest_commit/_bar_refusal/_review_bar_command/_run_review_bar/_unstaged_dirt\"\r\n+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/station.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py\"\r\n+code_symbol = \"RECORD_PREFIXES/fold_listing/tree_identity/refresh_subject/refresh_attestation/format_bar_green/bar_attestation/tests_digest/mechanical_close_attestation/work_tip/governing_rev/governing_identity/format_trailer/parse_trailer/round_file/session_log/format_scope/gating_span/filing_refusal/branch_paths/logged_rounds/round_entries/branch_entries/tree_already_judged/declared_phases/phases_owed/round_count/_closed_wi_ids/mechanical_close_subject/format_branch_trailer/branch_trailers;attest/_attest_preflight/_attest_message/_lane_off_trunk/_harness_floor_refusal/_attest_commit/_bar_refusal/_review_bar_command/_run_review_bar/_unstaged_dirt\"\r\n detail = \"\"\"tree_identity folds raw NUL-delimited `git ls-tree -r -z` entries after dropping docs/reviews/, docs/log.d/ and docs/iteration/, and returns a 64-hex SHA-256 identity. fold_listing accepts bytes and preserves every path byte so display quoting or decoding cannot merge distinct work trees. A Bar-Green attestation is exactly one column-0 label line, `Bar-Green: tree=<40 hex> work=<40 hex> bar=<review|landing|no-bar> tests=<64 hex|none> <summary>`; its verifier returns fields only when tree and work equal the commit's own tree and first parent and bar is in that set. tests carries none for an empty named test-path set; otherwise it carries the SHA-256 of that set after path separators and leading ./ are normalized, duplicates are removed, and the paths are joined in sorted order. Thus one set in any order or spelling has one value, and a different set has a different value. refresh_attestation admits a refresh subject only with that verified attestation and bar landing or no-bar, so work_tip never peels a review attestation as a refresh; the read-only identity walk still steps through any commit whose non-record identity equals its parent, including an empty review attestation. One producer writes every attestation: it fixes the staged tree before the bar, refuses a red bar or one that leaves the index or worktree off that tree, and restores the index on every failed write; its line joins the message's final trailer block. The attest route refuses before the bar when commit hooks are off, the primary checkout holds the branch, the worktree is dirty (including untracked files), the review-bar declaration is absent or empty, the message carries the label, or the harness floor refuses; it reads the review bar and named tests from the attested lane's own declarations, with no default. A trailer without bar is not read. work_tip peels only a verified refresh at the tip for the reset path; governing_rev is read-only and walks across commits whose non-record identity equals their first parent's, peeling any DISPOSABLE commit it meets to reach one those commits would otherwise hide, and ending at the first commit whose identity differs from its parent's or at its absent-parent and depth bounds - so a branch with no disposable commit under it still walks. TWO commit classes are disposable and the read-only walk peels BOTH: the station's REFRESH, admitted by refresh_attestation, and the machinery's OWN adjudication close, admitted by mechanical_close_attestation against exactly one parent and a no-renames changed-path stream lying wholly under docs/work/. That stream must pair deleted specs from exactly ONE docs/work/active/<branch>/ with additions of the same filenames under docs/work/complete/, and ONLY the move itself may create or destroy: an addition or deletion under docs/work/ that is not one half of a recognised move refuses the whole commit, since peeling it would measure a spec's injection or an archived row's destruction at the parent, where no reviewer saw it. Modifications ride along unrestricted, because a close's inbound relink rewrites other rows in place and only ever modifies. A mechanical close admits exactly one moved row; any other shape declines to peel toward more review. Its subject must equal the writer's composed subject exactly, so a public prefix/suffix with a forged middle is not an attestation. The commit that moved NOTHING is refused by that pairing rather than by a clause of its own: it names no source branch, and its empty id list composes a subject no real close carries. One property admits the two classes and it is not two rules: both are machine-authored end to end, and both move the tree without the lane having changed what it CLAIMS - docs/work/ is deliberately inside the identity because a spec's own claims are what a verdict is about, and the close carries those claims through unchanged. Every arm of both verifications fails toward REVIEW, since declining to peel measures at a later rev and can never ask for LESS - though not always for more: on the empty close the refused commit is identity-preserving, so the walk-through step reaches the same rev the peel would have, and the refusal guards this function's contract rather than any answer the gate gives. The two peels are NOT the same peel: work_tip calls refresh_attestation directly rather than through the shared disposable test, so a mechanical close is never removed by the destructive reset path, which may only ever drop a refresh sitting literally on the tip. governing_identity composes governing_rev and tree_identity for the branch tip or an explicit revision, including a round's reviewed commit and a trailer's carrier; the branch argument is a branch NAME, because the peel verifies a refresh commit against the branch it names and no refresh subject names HEAD. format_scope records a REVIEW session scope as full, narrow or final base..sha; gating_span admits a fresh full scope in either mode, or a final scope only where reviewer retention is on and final_reviewer is persisted; a narrow scope and a retained full scope never admit. logged_rounds joins branch-scoped round files to coordinator session logs by train and ordinal, and each round's review phase is the JOINED LOG's declared phase rather than the one its own filename carries, so a file cannot claim a phase its session did not serve; a joined key whose logs declare more than one review phase yields no round. It retains only a gating span whose base equals the caller's claim base and whose reviewed sha the round file names. round_entries retains only rounds whose reviewed revision governs the identity under judgement and emits phase, ordinal and verdict entries through an injected parser. filing_refusal applies one filing check: the first physical line is exactly the Reviewed full-sha opener (a CR ending is allowed; no leading blank or whitespace is), exactly one canonical VERDICT line, a finding count matching the file, and a change request naming a finding. An unreadable or refused round is an entry with no verdict, so it is the phase's latest word rather than an older verdict being used. tree_already_judged is true only for an entry carrying a verdict and false with no base. declared_phases clamps the configured independent-review count to the available review phases. phases_owed returns declared phases whose latest entry is missing or invalid evidence; a dissent is served. round_count returns the largest per-phase entry count at one governing identity, so a multi-phase review cycle counts once and changed work starts a new count. format_trailer and parse_trailer carry `Review-Verdict: APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED rounds=<N> tree=<64 hex>`. branch_trailers verifies each carrier against its governing identity and returns the ordered attestation sequence per tree. Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract.\"\"\"\r\n*** Update File: C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-977\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml\r\n@@\r\n automated = \"Yes\"\r\n-evidence = \"tests/test